                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who conducts or leads; a guide; a director."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfccf211-cfc4-49cf-9e09-03dc00e07005",
                                                "sense_id": "64a7c980-22a7-3d2c-9858-7575e1f58a06",
                                                "text": "[…]Zeal, the blind conductor of the will;"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "376de139-a00c-3ce7-8e8a-02d977122045",
                                        "entry_id": "7a6eece6-9a9a-30d8-9a71-62ef28797b3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who conducts an orchestra, choir or other music ensemble; a professional whose occupation is conducting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b92243d-288e-3a96-977a-0578a594c552",
                                        "entry_id": "7a6eece6-9a9a-30d8-9a71-62ef28797b3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who takes tickets on public transportation and also helps passengers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9eed42c5-d7fc-41d4-8fb2-95ea1ae2921b",
                                                "sense_id": "7b92243d-288e-3a96-977a-0578a594c552",
                                                "text": "train conductor"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "460086d8-dd12-4669-af50-c5a41a0e7bb6",
                                                "sense_id": "7b92243d-288e-3a96-977a-0578a594c552",
                                                "text": "tram conductor"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40f0e4e8-fa8a-4fe5-ba98-a5ccbd3de2d7",
                                                "sense_id": "7b92243d-288e-3a96-977a-0578a594c552",
                                                "text": "\"[…] And one of the things that makes me feel safe is when I see the conductor.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bdcb6ee8-ea19-357c-8574-025922039797",
                                        "entry_id": "7a6eece6-9a9a-30d8-9a71-62ef28797b3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that can transmit electricity, heat, light, or sound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "195cd47b-26c0-40f7-a8e1-83bcf60821fb",
                                                "sense_id": "bdcb6ee8-ea19-357c-8574-025922039797",
                                                "text": "Falling conductors may come in contact with grounded objects or puddles of water."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ddadb7e-b6a7-4d02-b015-a5daf5a739a0",
                                                "sense_id": "bdcb6ee8-ea19-357c-8574-025922039797",
                                                "text": "The failure of HIF detection leads to potential hazard to human beings and potential fire. HIFS are usually caused by falling conductors coming into contact with a surface having poor conductivity."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "245abbf3-bfde-31a9-b4eb-1d11f76967e6",
                                        "entry_id": "7a6eece6-9a9a-30d8-9a71-62ef28797b3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ideal of a ring that measures how far it is from being integrally closed"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d6d724df-f05e-4917-8d63-888a557fe40a",
                                                "sense_id": "245abbf3-bfde-31a9-b4eb-1d11f76967e6",
                                                "text": "If c is the conductor ideal for R in R then prime ideals not containing c correspond to localizations yielding discrete valuation rings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a929fe84-a2cf-3502-a264-b65edb10923e",
                                        "entry_id": "7a6eece6-9a9a-30d8-9a71-62ef28797b3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A grooved sound or staff used for directing instruments, such as lithontriptic forceps; a director."
                                        ],
